[Music]  okay so this is my spoiler free review  of the highly anticipated Amazon Prime  Show hunters which comes out Friday this  is actually held by David Weil who's  kind of a new face to the industry here  he is the showrunner creator of this and  he writes the first two episodes this is  also executive produced by Jordan Peele  who really can use a good produced show  in his belt after the disaster that was  Twilight Zone so when I got sent the  screeners I got sent five episodes so  I'm basing this off the first five this  is a ten episode season but with these  screeners came a note from David Weil he  was explaining how personal this story  is to him which got me very excited you  know it's coming from a place of deep  connection to the material there's  passion there you feel it in this letter  he wrote so I was really excited to dip  into this now let me just say the  premiere it's an hour and a half long it  could play as its own movie it is  spectacular the cinematography in this  episode alone felt game-changing on its  own it kind of felt like when I first  saw the cinematography in The Handmaid's  Tale or felt different it set such a  mood for the show and constantly kept  you on your feet in a good way not  distracting and this premiere has that I  mean you'll just notice it is a work of  art and how this cinematography is done  in this premiere episode so really take  it in and there's such heart to it it's  dark it's heavy-duty stuff in my head I  gave the premiere nine point eight I  thought it was almost perfect however  the person who directs the first episode  doesn't direct me into the other  episodes and you see the drop off and  also David wheel who is the creator and  main writer he does the first two  episodes and then dips out which always  frustrates me especially when it's your  first show you're really helming buying  you're saying it's personal to you write  the whole thing do a whole season why is  it that you only do two that really  frustrates me and you see the change in  quality in writing as well so as this  show goes on nothing comes close to  I saw on the premiere or maybe even the  tone I thought it was going to be it  goes from being just a very deep  personal story and unique in so many  ways to falling into another blend of  the boys and Watchmen and really any of  the Marvel Netflix type shows where it's  rated R type comic book story it's  gruesome but it's still hitting the same  plot points you got a detective here  who's in the middle of both sides with  these hunters and then these Nazis so  you're replacing really just super  heroes versus villains and it's this  group of Nazi hunters worse Nazis and  there's a detective trying to figure it  all out in the middle you've seen it  before it also is constantly quoting  comic books in the show that's clearly  inspired by but it gets tiresome in a  sense because we keep seeing this in so  many shows now the main gist of it being  about Nazi hunting is the unique part  but as it goes on you realize that's  really the most unique part of it all in  general it gets repetitive and a lot of  it you just feel like you've seen in  other shows just presented in a  different suit here I'm also very angry  when something seems like a complete  ripoff and this to me was actually with  the composer where if you were a big  leftovers fan you will notice there is  one song that the composer did here that  is a complete ripoff of one of the main  tunes of leftovers if you can catch that  let me know in the comments below I'd  love to see if you agree with me on that  cuz I think it's completely stolen and I  wasn't crazy about that it also suffers  from bloat I mean not one of these  episodes is under an hour they're long  it could definitely trim some fat here  it gets a little too self-indulgent in a  sense  I enjoyed that Ted Mosby from How I Met  Your Mother is getting work he's really  good as the comic relief here but he  still feels underwritten and that's  another problem I have where there's so  much weight given to the main character  but we have so many other characters and  in five episodes I still feel like I  haven't learned anything about them and  I still want to know more with more of  their character motivations and why  they're even doing what they're doing  so we'll see I mean I haven't seen the  next five so we'll see if that gets  sorted out now al pacino absolutely  kills it I thought he'd be one of those  things where he's in it for one episode  and disappears know he's ended a bunch  and he's great doesn't melt in one of  his best performances I've seen so it's  exciting to see him do this  the TV show the acting's good to all  across the board it's just certain  characters especially the lead character  here Jonah gets really annoying fast he  falls into that angsty teen branch but  more of like he's just a douche like you  don't like him and it's tough because  you started the most time with him he's  always angry and justice justifiably so  but to the point where the people should  even be nice to he's just awful and  annoying so that gets frustrating as  well  and a lot of the writing falls into that  writing that doesn't come off totally  natural here where a lot of characters  were just saying quotable things and I  say this a lot but it's like preaching  the sense of quotable things you'd hear  on Twitter that people say and a  character directly says this someone  you're like no one would ever say that  in a conversation so you fall into that  too and also in being a gruesome show  what was disappointing was the  choreography for the fighting it's  pretty stale it's not great I don't feel  any of the punches and I don't feel a  lot of these characters fight that well  so it's clearly got issues but I have a  feeling that this is a nice show in the  sense if you like comic book shows  you're gonna like this show it fits in  with the Daredevils of the world it fits  in with the boys it's good but if you're  looking for something that changes the  game and brings all audiences in it's  not this show it isn't the premiere  you're gonna watch from here and be like  wow this is incredible but you'll see as  it goes on it kind of just dips into  everything else you've kind of been  tuning in to accept the change being  okay we're doing nazi hunting which is  cool it's that's unique but I just wish  the way they presented it was more  unique in the end it's masking that  you're kind of seeing something you've  seen a hundred times over but overall  for the five episodes I saw I would give  this a solid eight point four it was one  of those shows was really hard to rate  because there was just points I'm  watching and I'm like the whole time  like do I really like this I don't know  like I'm being honest with you like  again I love the premiere and then after  that I was like I really want to like  this and I think it's okay I don't love  it it's not something I can sit there  and be like this is amazing  I feel like we're gonna say it's amazing  because you're excited at seeing these  new type of faces going on these new  type of villains you don't see  in this way in the comic book II  landscape of it it feels like it's based  off a comic and it isn't but underneath  all of that  it's formulaic and I just don't care  enough because it's just revenge revenge  revenge revenge and it loses its soul a  bit so we'll see maybe the last five  episodes bring it back up again  but that's why I'm gonna say four  hunters I definitely suggest if you like  that type of thing with comic book  check this out you're gonna dig it and  if you like it see you Nazis get killed  who doesn't you'll like it too but don't  expect this incredible show temper your  expectations after the premiere let me  know down below if you plan on watching  it I love to hear your thoughts please  make sure you subscribe to my channel I  review a bunch of TV shows I also do  celebrity interviews as well so you  don't wanna miss those and please follow  me at Steve arleigh 1 on Twitter and  scram for more of me I'll see you next  time

